`G a` is `g(χᵃ)^p`, the `p`-th power of the Gauss sum of `χᵃ` against a
primitive additive character of `F = 𝓞 CF ⧸ q`. The Gauss sum itself
lives in the compositum `L = CF(ζ_ℓ)`, `ℓ` the rational prime under
