set_option maxHeartbeats 1000000 in
/-- **The two spellings of "the local field at `q`" cut out CONJUGATE
subgroups of `Γℚ`** (E3c support leaf, cut 2026-07-27 out of
`exists_unramifiedAbelianSubgroup_relIndex_classGroup` below; PROVEN
2026-07-27 over `nonempty_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_padic` and
`exists_conj_map_of_ratRingEquiv` above): the image in `Γℚ` of the
absolute Galois group of
`HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletion ℚ v_q` is a `Γℚ`-CONJUGATE of the
image of the absolute Galois group of `ℚ_[q]`.

Both fields are "the" completion of `ℚ` at `q` — `ℚ_[q]` by
construction, `adicCompletion ℚ v_q` as the completion of `ℚ` for the
`v_q`-adic valuation — so they are isomorphic over `ℚ`. But
`Field.absoluteGaloisGroup.map` is built on an ARBITRARILY CHOSEN
embedding of algebraic closures (see its own docstring in
`AbsoluteGaloisGroup.lean`), and the two choices need not agree. Each
image is therefore the decomposition group at SOME place of `ℚ̄` above
`q`, and `Γℚ` permutes the places above `q` transitively, so the two
images are conjugate.

**EQUALITY IS FALSE IN GENERAL AND MUST NOT BE STATED HERE** — that is
the one trap in this leaf, and the conjugating `τ` is not decoration.
A first draft of this cut asserted equality; it is refuted by any
choice of the two embeddings landing on different places above `q`,
which nothing in the definitions forbids.

**Why it is needed.** `localSplitGenerators p` spells its `p`- and
`2`-disjuncts with `Γ ℚ_[p]` and `Γ ℚ_[2]`, whereas `localInertiaGroup`
and the inertia clause of
`exists_unramifiedAbelianSubgroup_relIndex_classGroup` below are
spelled with `Γ (adicCompletion ℚ v_ℓ)`. This leaf is exactly that
translation, and it is needed ONLY at `ℓ ∈ {2, p}`: at every other `ℓ`
the conjugated inertia element is a `localSplitGenerators` element on
the nose.

**The check that would refute it**: exhibit `q` and
`n : Γ (adicCompletion ℚ v_q)` whose image in `Γℚ` lies in no
`Γℚ`-conjugate of the image of `Γ ℚ_[q]`. Impossible: the image of `n`
lies in the decomposition group of the place induced by the chosen
embedding, and all places above `q` are `Γℚ`-conjugate.

**The route taken** is the one the cut anticipated as cheaper: build the
ring isomorphism `adicCompletion ℚ v_q ≃+* ℚ_[q]`
(`nonempty_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_padic`) and transport
(`exists_conj_map_of_ratRingEquiv`). Neither step ever produces an
equality of the two images, which is why the conjugator survives to the
statement. -/
theorem exists_padicAbsoluteGaloisGroup_conj_eq_map_adicCompletion
    (q : ℕ) [Fact q.Prime] (hq : q.Prime)
    (n : Field.absoluteGaloisGroup
      (IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletion ℚ
        hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat)) :
    ∃ (g : Field.absoluteGaloisGroup ℚ_[q]) (τ : Field.absoluteGaloisGroup ℚ),
      Field.absoluteGaloisGroup.map (algebraMap ℚ
        (IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletion ℚ
          hq.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat)) n =
      τ * Field.absoluteGaloisGroup.map (algebraMap ℚ ℚ_[q]) g * τ⁻¹ := by
  obtain ⟨E⟩ := nonempty_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_padic q hq
  exact exists_conj_map_of_ratRingEquiv q _ E n

/-- **Every `Γℚ`-conjugate of a local inertia element is a local-split
generator** (E3c support, 2026-07-27; PROVEN over
`exists_padicAbsoluteGaloisGroup_conj_eq_map_adicCompletion` above).

At `ℓ ∉ {2, p}` this is the first disjunct of `localSplitGenerators`
verbatim. At `ℓ = p` and at `ℓ = 2` the generating set carries the FULL
decomposition group rather than merely inertia, so an inertia element
is a generator a fortiori — modulo the change of spelling of the local
field, which is what the leaf above supplies, and modulo the conjugacy
`τ` it produces, which is absorbed into the conjugator `σ` of the
generator (`σ * (τ * x * τ⁻¹) * σ⁻¹ = (σ * τ) * x * (σ * τ)⁻¹`).

This lemma is the whole content of clause (c) of
`exists_unramifiedAbelianSubgroup_relIndex_classGroup` below: the
subgroup produced there is generated by conjugated inertia together
with the commutators of `ker χ`, and `localSplitSubgroup` is generated
by exactly those together with the two full decomposition groups, so
the inclusion is monotonicity of `Subgroup.closure` followed by
monotonicity of `Subgroup.topologicalClosure`. -/
theorem mem_localSplitGenerators_of_mem_localInertiaGroup
    (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime)
    (n : Field.absoluteGaloisGroup
      (IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletion ℚ
        hℓ.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat))
    (hn : n ∈ localInertiaGroup hℓ.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat)
    (σ : Field.absoluteGaloisGroup ℚ) :
    σ * Field.absoluteGaloisGroup.map (algebraMap ℚ
      (IsDedekindDomain.HeightOneSpectrum.adicCompletion ℚ
        hℓ.toHeightOneSpectrumRingOfIntegersRat)) n * σ⁻¹
      ∈ localSplitGenerators p := by
  by_cases h2 : ℓ = 2
  · subst h2
    obtain ⟨g, τ, hg⟩ :=
      exists_padicAbsoluteGaloisGroup_conj_eq_map_adicCompletion 2 hℓ n
    exact Or.inr (Or.inr ⟨g, σ * τ, by rw [hg, mul_inv_rev]; group⟩)
  · by_cases hq : ℓ = p
    · subst hq
      obtain ⟨g, τ, hg⟩ :=
        exists_padicAbsoluteGaloisGroup_conj_eq_map_adicCompletion ℓ hℓ n
      exact Or.inr (Or.inl ⟨g, σ * τ, by rw [hg, mul_inv_rev]; group⟩)
    · exact Or.inl ⟨ℓ, hℓ, h2, hq, n, hn, σ, rfl⟩

-- (`isOpen_localInertiaCommutatorSubgroup` is declared BELOW, after
-- `relIndex_localInertiaCommutatorSubgroup_eq_card_classGroup`, and it is PROVEN there.
-- Two branches worked this leaf concurrently: one hoisted a SORRIED copy to here and
-- built the class-field-theory chain below it, the other proved it in place over the
